{title: My Hope Is Built on Nothing Less}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
My [G]hope is built on [D]nothing less than [C]Jesus' blood and [G]righteousness
I [G]dare not trust the [D]sweetest frame, but [C]wholly lean in [G]Jesus' Name
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
On [G]Christ the solid [C]Rock I stand
All [G]other ground is [D]sinking sand
All [G]other ground is [D]sinking [<off>G</off>]sand.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [G]darkness veils his [D]lovely face, I [C]rest on His un[G]changing grace
In [G]every high and [D]stormy gale, my [C]anchor holds wi[G]thin the veil
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
His [G]oath, His cove[D]nant, His blood, sup[C]port me in the [G]whelming flood
When [G]all around my [D]soul gives way, He [C]then is all my [G]Hope and Stay
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 4}
When [G]He shall come with [D]trumpet sound; oh [C]may I then in [G]Him be found
Dressed [G]in His righteous[D]ness alone, fault[C]less to stand be[G]fore the throne
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

